{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"","sections":{"preamble":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.","tools":"<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n- grep: Search file contents for patterns (respects .gitignore)\n- find: Find files by glob pattern (respects .gitignore)\n- ls: List directory contents\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>","rules":"<rules>\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>","docs":"<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>","project_context":"<project_context>\nProject-specific instructions and guidelines:\n\n<project_instructions path=\"/app/AGENTS.md\">\n# AI Agent Guidelines (AGENTS.md) — Textualize/rich\n\n> Contributor and AI coding assistant guidelines for the **`Textualize/rich`** repository.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Philosophy & Architecture\n\nRich is a Python library for rich text and beautiful terminal formatting with zero non-standard runtime dependencies outside foundational typing and syntax parsers (`typing_extensions`, `pygments`, `markdown-it-py`).\n\n### Core Architectural Layers\n* **Console & Segments (`rich.console`, `rich.segment`)**:\n  - `Console` is the primary facade coordinating measurement, rendering, and terminal emission.\n  - `Segment` is the atomic rendering unit: a tuple of `(text: str, style: Optional[Style], control: Optional[ControlCode])`.\n* **Render Protocol (`rich.protocol`)**:\n  - Any renderable object implements `__rich_console__(self, console: Console, options: ConsoleOptions) -> RenderResult`.\n  - Generator method yielding `Segment` instances or nested renderables.\n  - Optional `__rich_measure__(self, console: Console, options: ConsoleOptions) -> Measurement` for computing minimum and maximum cell width.\n* **Style System (`rich.style`, `rich.color`, `rich.default_styles`)**:\n  - `Style` objects encapsulate ANSI SGR attributes (bold, italic, underline, color).\n  - Styles are immutable and combinable (`style1 + style2` or `Style.combine([s1, s2])`).\n  - Terminal themes map ANSI color names to RGB triplets.\n* **Layout & Data Structures (`rich.layout`, `rich.table`, `rich.panel`, `rich._ratio`)**:\n  - High-level containers (`Table`, `Panel`, `Columns`, `Tree`, `Layout`).\n  - `rich._ratio` provides mathematical solvers (`ratio_distribute`, `ratio_resolve`) for dividing available terminal cells among flexible and fixed-width components.\n* **Text & Markup (`rich.text`, `rich.markup`, `rich.highlighter`)**:\n  - `Text` manages character spans and styling offsets.\n  - `rich.markup` parses BBCode-like terminal markup (e.g., `[bold red]Alert[/]`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Engineering Standards & Conventions\n\n1. **Strict Type Annotations**:\n   - Every function, method parameter, and return type must have explicit Python type annotations (`typing`).\n   - Code must satisfy `mypy` without errors.\n2. **Pure Python & Zero Dependency Invariant**:\n   - Never introduce external third-party dependencies.\n   - Maintain compatibility across supported Python versions (3.8+).\n3. **Immutability & Stateless Rendering**:\n   - Do not mutate passed `ConsoleOptions` instances; use `options.update(...)` to derive child constraints.\n   - Never write directly to private console buffers (`console._buffer`). Always yield `Segment` instances.\n4. **Code Formatting**:\n   - Code adheres to standard `black` formatting and strict docstring conventions.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Testing & Verification Workflow\n\n`pytest` and all Rich dependencies are pre-installed in the environment. Always verify your changes using targeted `pytest` commands for the relevant module(s) before concluding your turn:\n\n```bash\n# Run ratio and table layout tests\npytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_table.py -q\n\n# Run styling and markup tests\npytest tests/test_style.py tests/test_markup.py -q\n\n# Run protocol and container tests\npytest tests/test_protocol.py tests/test_panel.py -q\n```\n\n</project_instructions>\n</project_context>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/app\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1794167743100,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"grep","description":"Search file contents for a pattern. Returns matching lines with file paths and line numbers. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 100 matches or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Long lines are truncated to 500 chars.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Search pattern (regex or literal string)"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory or file to search (default: current directory)"},"glob":{"type":"string","description":"Filter files by glob pattern, e.g. '*.ts' or '**/*.spec.ts'"},"ignoreCase":{"type":"boolean","description":"Case-insensitive search (default: false)"},"literal":{"type":"boolean","description":"Treat pattern as literal string instead of regex (default: false)"},"context":{"type":"number","description":"Number of lines to show before and after each match (default: 0)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of matches to return (default: 100)"}}}},{"name":"find","description":"Search for files by glob pattern. Returns matching file paths relative to the search directory. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 1000 results or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Glob pattern to match files, e.g. '*.ts', '**/*.json', or 'src/**/*.spec.ts'"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory to search in (default: current directory)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of results (default: 1000)"}}}},{"name":"ls","description":"List directory contents. Returns entries sorted alphabetically, with '/' suffix for directories. Includes dotfiles. Output is truncated to 500 entries or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory to list (default: current directory)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of entries to return (default: 500)"}}}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Component Implementation: Embeddable `Badge` UI Component\n\nProblem Description:\nDevelop a new visual status badge component `Badge` in `rich/badge.py` (and export it in `rich/__init__.py` and `rich.__all__`).\nThe component must be fully compatible with Rich's layout and rendering pipeline so that it can be printed directly via `console.print(badge)` or embedded seamlessly inside Tables, Panels, Columns, and Trees.\n\nArchitectural Standard:\nThe component must strictly adhere to the internal architectural conventions of this repository (as documented in the project Architecture Decision Records). It must implement the standard streaming render protocol and measurement protocol accepted in the codebase, properly handling standalone and nested layouts without breaking composition or accessing private console state.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Create `rich/badge.py`:\n   - Class `Badge`:\n     ```python\n     def __init__(\n         self,\n         text: str,\n         *,\n         style: StyleType = \"bold white on blue\",\n         border_style: StyleType = \"blue\",\n         pill: bool = True,\n         icon: Optional[str] = None,\n     ) -> None:\n     ```\n   - When `pill=True`, formats the badge with curved pill borders `( ` ... ` )`.\n   - When `pill=False`, formats with square borders `[ ` ... ` ]`.\n   - If `icon` is provided, includes `icon + \" \" + text`.\n   - Accurately reports cell measurement based on character cell lengths.\n2. In `rich/__init__.py`:\n   - Expose `Badge` in `__all__` and make it importable from the top-level `rich` package.\n3. Verification:\n   - Must comply with project architectural standards and render cleanly when printed standalone or nested inside Tables and Panels.\n   - All existing tests must continue to pass without regressions."}],"timestamp":1794167743099},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking the repo first, since AGENTS.md mentions ADRs. I'll look for a docs/adr directory to see if they're actually kept there.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll check the repo's ADRs and existing renderable patterns before writing the component."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01NRuoQx1eB2hyuH4EJyMM78","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && ls; find . -iname \"*adr*\" -not -path \"./.git/*\" | head; ls docs 2>/dev/null; cat rich/__init__.py | head -80; sed -n 1,60p rich/rule.py"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":4,"output":189,"cacheRead":1185,"cacheWrite":3672,"totalTokens":5050,"cost":{"input":4.0000000000000003e-7,"output":0.00009449999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00001185,"cacheWrite":0.000459,"total":0.00056575,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":39},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794167743128,"providerT